A command whose dead functions da in a.go and db in b.go each call helper, at
one byte of each file that a line directive renders at main.go:20:13. The kind
that would report helper is allowed, so explain lists both references.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}, "severity": {"DS1002": "allow"}}
-- a.go --
package main

//line main.go:20:1
func da() { helper() }
-- b.go --
package main

//line main.go:20:1
func db() { helper() }
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

func helper() {}
